Live-verified against AKI.IO 2026-08-24 (capture 5 of the karr #101 run, real key, 200 OK).

AKI.IO /anthropic/v1/messages returns tool_use blocks whose "input" is a JSON *string*,
not an object:

  {"type":"tool_use","id":"call_096bb7f8c49043adb6506902","name":"add",
   "input":"{\"a\": 7, \"b\": 15}"}

lib/Langertha/ToolCall.pm:89 (from_anthropic):

  arguments => ( ref( $block->{input} ) eq "HASH" ? $block->{input} : {} ),

The ": {}" branch is a SILENT fallback to empty. Replaying the captured body through
Engine::AKIAnthropic->chat_response yields:

  tool_calls : 1
     - id=call_096bb7f8c49043adb6506902 name=add
       arguments ref=HASH value={}          <-- 7 and 15 are gone

No croak, no warn. A Raider loop would invoke add() with no arguments and act on the
result. This is the worst failure shape: correct id, correct name, empty payload.

ASYMMETRY: from_openai (ToolCall.pm:77) handles exactly this case correctly via
_decode_args($fn->{arguments}) -- the OpenAI wire always ships arguments as a string, so
the decoder exists in the file already. from_anthropic never calls it because real
Anthropic ships input as an object.

Suggested fix: in from_anthropic, route a non-ref input through _decode_args, keep the
HASH branch as-is, and keep {} only for genuinely unusable input. Cheap and local.

Fixture available (verbatim capture, real server values):
  akianthropic_tool_call_response.json  -- also carries a thinking block with a signature
Gate the fix with it rather than a hand-written payload (that is the whole point of #101).

Discovered by the live probe requested in karr #102. Engine built in #89 (closed as done)
was never tool-tested -- its POD called the tool path unverified, correctly so.

Fixed in 2653715: from_anthropic routes input through _decode_args (symmetric with from_openai); gated by a value-object unit test using the k124 captured tool_use block. Engine-level fixture replay (akianthropic_tool_call_response.json) belongs to k101 fixture infra which is not yet in the repo.

Orchestrator review 2026-09-01: diff 2653715 verified. _decode_args passes HASH through, decodes strings, {} only for unusable input; unit test covers the k124 capture shape. prove -lr t/ green (3146 tests), perlcritic clean. Closing.
